      "source": "The slides identify mass as the hardest listed stellar property to measure and use Doppler shifts in binary stars to study orbital motion. Brightness and spectra provide temperature and luminosity clues; an orbit supplies gravitational information needed to constrain masses. The label “spectroscopic parallax” refers to a distance estimate from stellar properties, not a direct annual angular parallax measurement.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"study-points\"><li>The slides identify mass as the hardest listed stellar property to measure and use <mark class=\"study-term\">Doppler shifts</mark> in <mark class=\"study-term\">binary stars</mark> to study orbital motion.<ul class=\"study-subpoints\"><li>Brightness and spectra provide temperature and luminosity clues.</li><li>An orbit supplies gravitational information needed to constrain masses.</li></ul></li><li>The label “<mark class=\"study-term\">spectroscopic parallax</mark>” refers to a distance estimate from stellar properties, not a direct annual angular parallax measurement.</li></ul>"
